}
```

The condition is checked before every pass, exactly like a for loop's middle part — the difference is there's no built-in counter managing it. Whatever needs to change to eventually make the condition false has to be handled explicitly inside the body, by you. In the spoons example, `spoonsLeft = spoonsLeft - 1;` is doing that work — without it, nothing about the loop's situation would ever change.

