contentSections.body:
Once you've sorted what varies from what doesn't, the extraction itself is mechanical:

```
function logSymptom(symptomName, severity) {
  console.log(`Symptom: ${symptomName}, severity: ${severity}`);
}

logSymptom("fatigue", 7);
logSymptom("brain fog", 5);
logSymptom("joint pain", 8);
```

Three lines became four (the definition plus three calls), which can look like more code, not less — but from here on, changing the wording of the message means editing it in exactly one place, not three, and adding a fourth symptom is one short call instead of one more full line to get right.

